    history_html: `<p><strong>2018:</strong> Epic Seven launched with a 30-pull hard pity system from inception. Smilegate positioned the game as player-friendly despite competitive RPG monetization trends, emphasizing story quality and fairness.</p><p><strong>2020:</strong> The game introduced equipment summoning with its own pity mechanics, creating optional but rewarding gear optimization without fragmenting character summoning resources excessively.</p><p><strong>2021-2022:</strong> Smilegate published detailed future banner schedules and increased free currency distribution in response to community feedback. The transparency and player-respect approach solidified the game's reputation.</p><p><strong>2023:</strong> Epic Seven received major content updates focusing on new story chapters and quality-of-life improvements. The game remained one of the fairest and most story-rich gachas available.</p><p><strong>2024-Present:</strong> Epic Seven maintains stable monetization with consistent content updates. The game is cited by industry advocates as a model for ethical gacha design balancing profitability and player welfare.</p>`,
    controversy_html: `<p>Epic Seven experienced minimal monetization controversies. The primary complaint comes from occasional balance concerns where newly released heroes are slightly stronger than predecessors. Smilegate addresses these through character buffs and balance passes rather than forcing recollection.</p><p>A minor controversy emerged around cosmetic pricing (skins costing premium currency), but cosmetics are entirely optional and provide zero gameplay advantage. This is standard practice and not considered predatory.</p>`,
    tips_html: `<p><strong>1. Plan for 30-pull pity:</strong> Save 3,000 Mystic Medals (~3 weeks of free rewards) before summoning limited character banners. The 30-pull guarantee provides budget predictability.</p><p><strong>2. Check published schedules before pulling:</strong> Smilegate releases 3-month character schedules regularly. If your desired hero isn't featured soon, wait for their scheduled rerun rather than pulling on current banners.</p><p><strong>3. Maximize daily free currency:</strong> The game awards 1-2 free pulls daily through logins and weeklies. These compound to 30-60 free pulls monthly, covering most of one guaranteed hero.</p><p><strong>4. Build gear gradually through free sources:</strong> Equipment gacha is optional for casual play. Obtain gear through story and event rewards before considering premium summoning for optimization.</p><p><strong>5. Engage story content fully:</strong> Story campaigns yield substantial free Mystic Medals per chapter. Prioritize story progression over grinding—it provides free currency and narrative enjoyment simultaneously.</p>`,
    editorial_html: `<p>Epic Seven demonstrates that 30-pull pity, published schedules, and story depth create engaging gacha experiences without sacrificing fairness. The transparency score of 8/10 reflects clear rate disclosure, visible pity counters, and published future schedules. The fairness score of 7/10 acknowledges hard pity and generous free currency while noting newer heroes receive soft stat advantages in competitive modes.</p><p>The game's story quality is exceptional—narrative-driven gameplay is rare in gachas where stories are often afterthoughts. This gameplay advantage combined with fair monetization creates strong overall value. The artwork and animation quality also distinguish it from competitors.</p><p>The value proposition is strong across all spending tiers. F2P players obtain limited heroes monthly through free currency. Casual spenders ($5-10/month) secure most limited releases. Whales can pursue cosmetics and gear optimization, but no mandatory power gates exist.</p><p>Recommendation: Epic Seven is recommended for narrative-focused RPG fans and fairness advocates. The combination of story depth, artistic quality, and ethical monetization is rare. F2P players should engage confidently. Casual spenders maximize value easily. Whales appreciate transparent design. If you want a story-rich gacha with fair monetization, this is your game.</p>`,
