    tips_html: `<p><strong>1. Save for 25-pull guaranteed:</strong> Accumulate 2,500 Quartz (~2-3 weeks of free rewards) before summoning limited character banners. This guarantees the featured character and prevents wasted currency.</p><p><strong>2. Plan using published schedules:</strong> Nexon releases detailed future banner roadmaps. Check upcoming characters before summoning—if your desired character is 2 weeks away, wait rather than pull now.</p><p><strong>3. Maximize daily free Quartz:</strong> The game awards 1-2 free pulls daily through logins and weeklies. These compound to 30-40 free summons monthly, covering most of one guaranteed character.</p><p><strong>4. Engage story content fully:</strong> Main story and limited-time story events yield substantial free Quartz. Prioritize story progression for free currency and narrative enjoyment simultaneously.</p><p><strong>5. Focus PvE campaigns:</strong> Campaign content is entirely clearable with free and low-cost characters. Avoid competitive PvP if budget-constrained—it's optional.</p>`,
    editorial_html: `<p>KonoSuba: Fantastic Days proves that anime license gachas can achieve fairness without sacrificing appeal. The transparency score of 7/10 reflects explicit pity counters, published rates, and future schedules. The fairness score of 7/10 acknowledges the 25-pull pity, aggressive free currency (25+ monthly pulls), and PvE-focused design creating minimal mandatory spending pressure.</p><p>The game's strength is anime faithfulness—the story respects the source material while providing original content. Gameplay quality is solid tactical RPG, and character designs are authentic to the anime. For franchise fans, this legitimacy matters significantly.</p><p>The value proposition is excellent for anime fans. F2P players obtain limited characters monthly. Casual spenders ($5-10/month) secure most releases. Whales appreciate character variety and cosmetics. The game prioritizes fan enjoyment over extraction.</p><p>Recommendation: KonoSuba: Fantastic Days is recommended for KonoSuba fans seeking fair gacha monetization. The 25-pull pity and published schedules eliminate FOMO-driven spending pressure. F2P players should play confidently. Casual spenders maximize value. Even whales appreciate transparent design. For anime fans tired of predatory monetization, this is a breath of fresh air. Strongly recommended.</p>`,
